Azure architecture decisions frequently involve tradeoffs. Improving one characteristic of a workload can sometimes increase cost, complexity, or operational requirements.

Common tradeoffs include:

* Performance versus cost
* Availability versus complexity
* Security versus convenience
* Scalability versus resource consumption
* Redundancy versus expenditure

For example, deploying an application across multiple Azure regions can improve resilience but introduces additional infrastructure, networking, and operational costs.

A real-life use case is a startup deciding whether its early-stage application actually requires multi-region deployment or whether a highly available single-region architecture is sufficient.

Good cloud architecture does not attempt to maximize every characteristic independently. Instead, it balances technical requirements against business priorities.
